  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0113_f72e931695f4.png\" style=\"width: 544px; height: 340px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HBr</mi></math>&nbsp;attacks on given molecule and provides product in which&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>Br</mi></math>&nbsp;group is attached at two sites (one is substitution and another is addition on alkene ) and it is followed by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;elimination and provides alkene which gives aldehyde on ozonolysis.</p>"
